A policy engine for files of any language: Rego policies over data formats, code, and the code embedded in either - awk in a shell string, shell in a YAML `run:`

Usage: zoll [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  check      Check files against the policies
  inspect    Print the input a policy sees for a file and for each fragment in it
  lock       Pin each git policy source to its commit in `zoll.lock`
  languages  List the languages zoll parses
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --config <PATH>  This config instead of the one found from the working directory up
      --color <WHEN>   When to color the output [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -h, --help           Print help
  -V, --version        Print version
